# 130. Final Architecture Principle

The infrastructure of AEGIS must embody one rule:

> **Every important system capability must have a defined place to run, a defined way to communicate, a defined way to fail, a defined way to recover, and a defined way to be observed.**

That is what turns an architecture document into an operational system.

AEGIS should therefore never reach the stage where the team says:

```text
"We built the application.
Now let's figure out deployment."
```

Deployment is part of the architecture.

Security is part of the architecture.

Recovery is part of the architecture.

Observability is part of the architecture.

Testing is part of the architecture.

The infrastructure must be designed alongside the product rather than attached to it at the end.
